{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem (parity sibling of the tickets-branch invariant violation)\nTwo more tickets-branch writers bypass the shared store seams and the two-part invariant\n(under the unified write lock + auto-commit/publish), same class as projects_store\n(ticket fea4-f98c-f1a2-4168, LANDED):\n1. reconcile_helpers._commit_binding_store_snapshot (reconcile_helpers.py:169) commits\n   .bridge_state binding/rotation/link state via raw git_adapter.add + commit. git_adapter\n   imports only rebar._store.gitutil.run_git — it does NOT acquire rebar._store.lock.write_lock,\n   so it races the ticket-CLI _push_tickets_branch() and concurrent GHA commit-back (the\n   exact race the write lock exists to prevent).\n2. alert_store._atomic_write (alert_store.py:84) hand-rolls tempfile+os.replace instead of\n   the shared rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write seam.\n\n## Use the EXISTING seams (NO new facade, NO redesign) — same as ticket fea4\n- rebar._store.push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, *, message=...) — stages ALL\n  pending tracker changes with `git add -A`, commits them under the unified write lock\n  (+ rebase guard), then pushes. This mirrors the GHA commit-back step and is exactly the\n  seam fea4 adopted for projects_store.\n- rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write — the shared crash-atomic write.\n\n## Approach\n### 1. _commit_binding_store_snapshot -> commit_and_push_tickets_branch (INTENTIONAL widening)\nReplace the raw git_adapter add/commit (and the selective 5-file staging + per-file\nidempotency logic it currently hand-rolls: bindings.json, bindings-retired.json,\nget_rotation.json, impossible_links.json, peer_confirmations.json) with a single call to\npush.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker_dir, message=..., strict=True) INSIDE the\nexisting try/except.\n- This is NOT a claim of committed-file-set equivalence. The seam stages `git add -A`, so it\n  commits ALL pending changes in the .tickets-tracker worktree under the lock, which is a\n  deliberate WIDENING from the prior selective staging and the intended parity behavior\n  (identical to GHA commit-back and to the landed fea4 conversion of projects_store).\n- Why the widening is safe / behavior-preserving in substance: the reconciler's\n  .tickets-tracker worktree only ever holds tickets-branch state — ticket events are already\n  auto-committed by the store, so the only files that can be pending here are .bridge_state\n  artifacts that BELONG on the tickets branch anyway (binding stores, get_rotation,\n  impossible_links, peer_confirmations, projects.json, prev_snapshot, last-pass). `git add -A`\n  therefore never commits a file that should not be on the tickets branch; at worst it lands\n  an already-tickets-branch file (e.g. a rare pending operator projects.json write) in the\n  same locked commit instead of a later one. This widening is PINNED by a test (see Testing),\n  not asserted away.\n- Fail-open PRESERVED: strict=True raises PushDeliveryError on any local/commit/push failure;\n  the existing except catches it, logs the same stderr line, appends the same\n  binding-commit-failure alert, and returns False — the pass never aborts. On success return\n  True. A clean tree is a no-op commit (no-op-when-clean idempotency preserved). A\n  retirement-only change still makes the tree dirty, so it still commits (bug 1e08 outcome\n  preserved).\n\n### 2. alert_store._atomic_write -> fsutil.atomic_write (RESIDENCY = LOCAL SCRATCH)\nalert_store writes to repo_root/bridge_state/bridge_alerts (NO dot), which .gitignore\n('bridge_state/') ignores and which is NOT tracked on the tickets branch (only the dotted\n.bridge_state/* is). So the alert files are local scratch: fsutil.atomic_write ALONE is\ncorrect — NO publish/commit path is added.\n- IMPORTANT: current _atomic_write does parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True) before\n  writing; fsutil.atomic_write does NOT create the destination directory. So KEEP an explicit\n  path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True) immediately before the fsutil.atomic_write\n  call, then call fsutil.atomic_write(path, content, permissions=0o600, fsync=True) to\n  preserve exact serialized bytes, mode 0o600 (mkstemp default, no chmod today), and the\n  fsync-before-replace durability.\n\n## Constraints — BEHAVIOR-PRESERVING\nNo functional change beyond lock+seam adoption: same fail-open on commit error, same\nno-op-when-clean, same on-disk alert bytes/mode. Reuse existing seams ONLY; add no helper.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- RED-first. _commit_binding_store_snapshot: patch push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch (NOT\n  subprocess) and assert (a) it is invoked with the tracker_dir and strict=True; (b) a raised\n  PushDeliveryError yields fail-open (returns False, pass not aborted, binding-commit-failure\n  alert appended); (c) success returns True; (d) the INTENDED widening is pinned — when an\n  unrelated pending .bridge_state file (e.g. projects.json) exists, it is included in the\n  single locked commit (documents that git add -A commits all pending tickets-branch state).\n- alert_store: byte-identity test that fsutil.atomic_write produces the same file contents and\n  0o600 mode as before, and that the write succeeds when the parent dir does not pre-exist\n  (guards the retained mkdir).\n- Re-point existing tests coupled to the removed selective-staging mechanism at the seam:\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_commit_binding_store_failure.py,\n  test_binding_retired_commit.py, test_get_rotation_commit_heldout.py,\n  test_binding_commit_survives_merge.py, test_git_adapter_characterization.py, AND\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py,\n  test_impossible_links_cicada.py.\n- Proving commands (all must pass): `make lint`; `make typecheck`;\n  `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ -q` (modulo the known-unrelated\n  state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote flake).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] _commit_binding_store_snapshot routes through push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch\n      (tracker_dir, message=..., strict=True); the raw git_adapter add/commit + selective\n      staging is removed; fail-open (returns False + appends binding-commit-failure alert on\n      PushDeliveryError, pass not aborted) and no-op-when-clean are preserved and pinned by a\n      test that patches the seam.\n- [ ] The intended `git add -A` widening is pinned by a test showing an unrelated pending\n      .bridge_state file is committed in the same locked commit (no silent non-tickets-branch\n      file is ever swept).\n- [ ] alert_store._atomic_write is replaced by fsutil.atomic_write with a retained\n      parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True); residency determined = local scratch\n      (documented); no publish path; exact bytes + 0o600 mode + fsync preserved; pinned by a\n      byte-identity test that also covers the missing-parent-dir case.\n- [ ] No functional/behavioral change beyond lock+seam adoption.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ -q`\n      all pass (modulo the known-unrelated state/test_ref_lock.py flake).\n\n## Sequencing\nDepends on fea4 (LANDED). Edits reconcile_helpers.py + alert_store.py (+ tests) — disjoint\nfrom A/C/D."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786821954290841001,"uuid":"64d06f63-f5f6-4fa3-9579-340aa967f380"}